node_modules/
dist/
src/styles/tokens.generated.css
*.local
.DS_Store
tmp/
public/generated/sol-staking-market-cache.json
# Market-conditions cache IS committed, like stable-yield-market-cache.json beside it.
# It used to be ignored, on the plan that `npm run build:deploy` would regenerate it from
# the server-side key before every build. That is not what deploys actually run: production
# served the SPA's index.html for this path, so the app had no market reading at all and
# every target allocation fell back to `degraded_market_excluded`, silently — the visible
# caption for that state was removed in MCC-5. The refresh workflow also contradicted the
# rule outright, committing and pushing this exact file, which is why it failed with
# "exists on disk, but not in 'HEAD'" the moment it got far enough to try.
# Committing it means the deployed build always carries a reading, whatever the pipeline does.
public/generated/*.tmp
dist-server/
